r a large variety                                                                wide range of possibilities for detailed studies of the nu-\n\f                                                                                                                         13\n\n                                                               hadroproduction processes, encompassing the study of\nTABLE VIII: Same as in Tab. IV but now at LO accuracy.\n                                                               the spin and flavor structure with polarized SIDIS mea-\nexperiment         data     rel. norm. data points     χ2      surements [26], in proton-proton collisions [27], and in\n                   type        in fit     fitted               photoproduction [28], the modification of parton densi-\n                                                               ties by nuclear effects [29], or studies of high pT electro-\nTPC [2]            incl.       1.041        17         7.7\n                                                               production processes [30].\nSLD [3]            incl.       1.014        21        63.0\nALEPH [4]          incl.       1.013        27        46.4\nDELPHI [5]         incl.        1.0         12       12.2\n                “uds tag”       1.0         12        22.3                         Acknowledgments\n                  “b tag”       1.0         12        16.6\nTASSO [11] incl. (44 GeV)       1.0         14       22.3         We warmly acknowledge Werner Vogelsang for help-\n             incl. (35 GeV)     1.0         14        56.3     ful discussions, and Carlos Garcı́a Canal for comments\n                                                               and suggestions. This work was partially supported by\nOPAL [12]          incl.        1.0         12       28.5\n                                                               CONICET, ANPCyT and UBACyT.\n                “uds tag”       1.0         12        32.9\n                